WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:03.000
Hi, I'm Grommet!

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.731
TorchTPU runs ordinary PyTorch on Google's TPUs, as a real device.

00:00:09.558 --> 00:00:13.435
The idea: every op gets a TPU kernel, and a policy decides

00:00:13.435 --> 00:00:15.050
when to compile and launch.

00:00:18.275 --> 00:00:21.632
The old path recorded ops into a graph and compiled at a

00:00:21.632 --> 00:00:22.751
step boundary you marked.

00:00:23.448 --> 00:00:25.742
TorchTPU is a device in the dispatcher.

00:00:25.742 --> 00:00:28.692
Eager runs op by op; deferring is a choice.

00:00:30.425 --> 00:00:33.740
An op on a tpu tensor reaches a kernel registered under

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:34.945
the private use key.

00:00:35.365 --> 00:00:37.740
That kernel builds a tiny StableHLO function.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:40.115
There are about four hundred and forty.

00:00:40.535 --> 00:00:42.604
In defer and fuse mode nothing runs.

00:00:42.604 --> 00:00:44.673
The tensor points at a deferred op.

00:00:45.093 --> 00:00:48.620
When Python reads a value, the region it needs becomes a cache key.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.325
A miss compiles once.

00:00:50.325 --> 00:00:53.216
A hit launches the cached program on the TPU.

00:00:54.942 --> 00:00:56.485
Four modes share those kernels.

00:00:57.531 --> 00:01:00.591
Strict launches each op and lets the CPU run ahead.

00:01:01.011 --> 00:01:02.427
Debug waits for every op.

00:01:03.053 --> 00:01:06.752
Defer and fuse waits for a read, then runs one fused program.

00:01:07.172 --> 00:01:10.121
Torch compile replays a whole graph through the same deferral.

00:01:11.758 --> 00:01:14.349
PyTorch and JAX both emit StableHLO.

00:01:14.349 --> 00:01:16.940
Pallas kernels enter lower, as Mosaic.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:21.440
Below that is one XLA compiler, down to a TPU executable.

00:01:22.842 --> 00:01:25.071
The numbers check out, with a catch.

00:01:25.071 --> 00:01:28.893
Two posts quote different efficiency for one run: one charges attention for

00:01:28.893 --> 00:01:30.803
the half a causal mask skips.

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:36.539
Remember: the new part is when to compile, and every mode shares one lowering.

00:01:40.275 --> 00:01:44.969
A kernel per op, work deferred until read, and check how efficiency counts attention.

00:01:45.389 --> 00:01:47.437
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:47.437 --> 00:01:48.022
I'm Grommet.

00:01:48.022 --> 00:01:48.315
Bye!
